  "reconstruction": {
    "scope": "Specific restored St Urban Tower in Kosice: pale-plaster square body/floor bands, small closed windows, genuinely open round-arched upper belfry, simple original roundel frieze, steep flared pyramidal brown tiled roof/vent/gilt ball/iron finial, low open round-arched arcade with two rounded western corners/red-brown roofs and selected central portal relief. Existing shared low-frequency stucco/stone/roof/paint graphs; no copied epitaphs, heraldry, inscriptions, photographs, museum interior, temporary restoration fence, neighboring cathedral or whole square platform.",
    "identityBasis": "Retained exact-QID OSMway25720529 and native parent35184397809361/core35185247715697/five arcade parts identify the tower. Native core quadrilateral supplies internal axes/center[0.25360674849280684,0.15650602748593623]m at anchor21.258135114,48.7206616. The older reference point is offset and does not control placement. Global heading0/native east-south retains mapped footprint; the west-side rounded arcade corners and central portal follow pictures/outline. Fine facade/reverse layout retains20degree/2m uncertainty.",
    "heightBasis": "Retained parent height1 also appears on the native parent. Native core child has44m and five low arcade children5m. Preserve these distinct attributes;1m is not a plausible overall height or proof of a measured1m foundation. Use44m overall model envelope with picture-led allocations for the core/roof/finial and5m low-arcade roof envelope. Actual architecture/engineering remains approximate. Nominal plaster/eave32.1m, curved pyramid to42.2m, gilt ball and iron finial to44m; low arcade eave3.35m/top5m. Floor-band/window/frieze/portal inventory and allocations remain picture-led estimates, not surveyed conservation dimensions.",
    "terrainBasis": "Retain original6m standard Mapzen terrain, native streets/paths/water and independent cathedral/surrounding buildings. Replace only seven corresponding native tower/arcade records. Bounded buried tower/arcade feet and narrow occupied arcade floors meet the coarse grid; no full-square slab, terrain flattening or ground/water cutout. Arcade openings extend to their occupied floors, and the upper belfry is hollow. Foundation/floor datum and obscured lower works remain coarse-map estimates.",
